[00:01.00]It came upon the midnight clear,
[00:06.50]That glorious song of old,
[00:12.00]From angels bending near the earth
[00:17.50]To touch their harps of gold:
[00:23.00]Peace on the earth, good will to men,
[00:28.50]From heaven's all-gracious King.
[00:34.00]The world in solemn stillness lay
[00:39.50]To hear the angels sing.
[00:46.00]Still through the cloven skies they come
[00:51.50]With peaceful wings unfurled,
[00:57.00]And still their heavenly music floats
[01:02.50]O'er all the weary world;
[01:08.00]Above its sad and lowly plains
[01:13.50]They bend on hovering wing,
[01:19.00]And ever o'er its Babel sounds
[01:24.50]The blessed angels sing.
